LESS(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    less - page through text with navigation and regex search

SYNOPSIS
    less [-RNS] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    Loads logical lines so pipes can be navigated backwards. With redirected
    output, copies the input unchanged. -R passes SGR colours through while
    excluding their bytes from display width. -N shows line numbers.
    -S truncates long lines; < and > move horizontally in eight-column steps.
    Space/f moves a page forward, b back, j/Enter a line down, k up,
    g to the start and G to the last page. / searches forward and ? backward
    using extended regular expressions; n repeats and N reverses direction.
    Type a number followed by % to jump to a percentage. q or Ctrl-C quits.
    The terminal mode is restored on exit.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
